-- Inputs spelled like a FEEL function the export calls. FEEL looks up a
-- call's name among the variables first, so before these names were reserved
-- an input named `floor` made `floor(x)` a call of the number the input
-- holds, and KIE refused all three decisions at run time ("Not an
-- invocable"). Each input is now emitted with a suffix (`floor_`), and its
-- label keeps the L4 name.
IMPORT prelude

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      floor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `f` x floor IS max (FLOOR x) floor

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      decimal IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `g` y decimal IS ROUND y PLUS decimal

GIVEN items IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      concatenate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `h` items concatenate IS sum items PLUS concatenate
